---
title: Sequence Diagram — Spring Security Filter Chain (JWT Validation)
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor Client as 👤 Client (Browser/Postman)
    participant CORS as CorsFilter
    participant CSRF as CsrfFilter<br/>(Disabled)
    participant JWT as JwtAuthenticationFilter<br/>(OAuth2ResourceServer)
    participant JWKS as Keycloak JWKS<br/>(Public Keys Cache)
    participant CONV as KeycloakRoleConverter
    participant AUTH as AuthorizationFilter<br/>(@PreAuthorize)
    participant CTRL as UserController
    participant EXC as ExceptionTranslationFilter

    Note over Client,EXC: Request: PUT /api/v1/users/{id}<br/>Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiI...

    Client->>CORS: Request with Origin header
    CORS->>CORS: Check allowed origins<br/>http://localhost:3000 ✅
    CORS->>CSRF: Pass through

    CSRF->>CSRF: Disabled (stateless JWT)<br/>Skip CSRF check
    CSRF->>JWT: Pass through

    JWT->>JWT: Extract token from<br/>Authorization: Bearer header
    JWT->>JWT: Decode JWT header<br/>→ kid: "key-abc", alg: "RS256"

    JWT->>JWKS: Get public key for kid: "key-abc"
    Note right of JWKS: First request: fetch from<br/>http://keycloak:8180/.../certs<br/>Subsequent: use cached key
    JWKS-->>JWT: RSA Public Key

    JWT->>JWT: Verify signature ✅<br/>Check expiry (exp) ✅<br/>Check issuer (iss) ✅

    JWT->>CONV: Convert JWT claims to authorities
    CONV->>CONV: Extract realm_access.roles<br/>→ ["EDITOR"]
    CONV->>CONV: Add ROLE_ prefix<br/>→ [ROLE_EDITOR]
    CONV-->>JWT: GrantedAuthorities

    JWT->>JWT: Create JwtAuthenticationToken<br/>{principal: JWT, authorities: [ROLE_EDITOR]}
    JWT->>JWT: Set SecurityContext

    JWT->>AUTH: Authenticated request
    AUTH->>AUTH: Evaluate @PreAuthorize<br/>"hasRole('ADMIN') or #id == @securityUtils.currentUserId"
    
    alt User is updating OWN profile
        AUTH->>AUTH: #id == currentUserId → TRUE ✅
        AUTH->>CTRL: Allow access
        CTRL-->>Client: 200 OK + Updated User
    else User is NOT admin AND NOT own profile
        AUTH->>EXC: Access Denied
        EXC-->>Client: 403 Forbidden<br/>{"error": "Access Denied"}
    end

    Note over Client,EXC: If NO token provided:
    Note over JWT,EXC: JWT filter → No Bearer token found → 401 Unauthorized
